            sometimes denoted simply by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r(B|x)
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r'(B|x)
          %p
            This kernel satisfies the property that for every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in\mathcal{A}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\in\mathcal{B}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi A
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\int_A r'(B|x) \, p(d x) = r(A\times B) ,
          %p and is therefore a generalization of conditional probability to the non-discrete setting. Compare it to the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  P(b|a)\,P(a) = P(a,b) .
          %h2#categories_of_markov_kernels Categories of Markov kernels
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stoch"} Stoch
                is the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+spaces"} measurable spaces
                and Markov kernels between them.
            %li
              %p
                One can also form the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+spaces"} probability spaces
                and equivalence classes of Markov kernels between them (under
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+kernel#almost_sure_equality"} almost sure equality
            %li
              %p
                One can restrict the category above to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel"} standard Borel
                probability spaces, obtaining a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+category"} dagger category
                sometimes denoted by
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krn"} Krn
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+couplings"} category of couplings
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
